<article>
	<h1><span>Storefront: Options</span></h1>

	<ul class="nav">
		<li><a href="#overview">Overview</a></li>
		<li><a href="#column-headers">Column Headers</a></li>
		<li><a href="#toolbar">Toolbar</a></li>
		<li><a href="#sub-menu">Sub-menu Links</a></li>
	</ul>

	<section id="overview">
		<h2><span>Overview</span></h2>

		<p>This screen lists the options of one option group. It opens from the <strong>Option Groups</strong>
			list.</p>
		<p>The heading of the list reads &quot;Options for:&quot; followed by the name of the option group. The name
			links to the editing screen of the option group.</p>
	</section>
	<section id="column-headers">
		<h2><span>Column Headers</span></h2>

		<dl>
			<dt>Checkbox</dt>
			<dd>Check this box to select one or more items. To select all items, check the box in the column heading.
				After one or more boxes are checked, click a toolbar button to take an action on the selected item or
				items. Publish, Unpublish and Delete work with multiple items. Edit only works on one item at a time.
				If multiple items are checked and you press Edit, the first item will be opened for editing.</dd>

			<dt>Title</dt>
			<dd>The name of the option. If you may edit options, the name links to the option's editing screen.</dd>

			<dt>Published</dt>
			<dd>Shows whether the option is Published, Unpublished or Trashed. If you may change the state, click
				the icon to publish an unpublished or trashed option, or to unpublish a published one.</dd>
		</dl>
	</section>
	<section id="toolbar">
		<h2><span>Toolbar</span></h2>
		<p>At the top right you will see the toolbar.</p>
		<p>The functions are:</p>
		<dl>
			<dt>Options</dt>
			<dd>Opens the Storefront configuration options in a pop-up window.</dd>

			<dt>Publish</dt>
			<dd>Publishes the selected options.</dd>

			<dt>Unpublish</dt>
			<dd>Unpublishes the selected options.</dd>

			<dt>New</dt>
			<dd>Opens the editing screen to create a new option in this option group.</dd>

			<dt>Edit</dt>
			<dd>Opens the editing screen for the selected option. If more than one option is selected, only the first
				one will be opened. The editing screen can also be opened by clicking on the <strong>Title</strong> of
				the option.</dd>

			<dt>Delete</dt>
			<dd>Opens a confirmation screen for the selected options. Check &quot;I'm positive. Go ahead and do the
				delete.&quot; and press <strong>Next</strong> to delete them. Pressing Next without the check cancels
				the delete.</dd>

			<dt>Help</dt>
			<dd>Opens this help screen.</dd>
		</dl>
	</section>
	<section id="sub-menu">
		<h2><span>Sub-menu Links</span></h2>
		<p>At the top left, you will see sub-menu options. The links are:</p>
		<dl>
			<dt>Products</dt>
			<dt>Collections</dt>
			<dt>Option Groups</dt>
		</dl>
	</section>
</article>
